[{:db/id "q-37778/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "be5d68ff-5a62-5dff-87bd-3f8d07976020" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37778/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "11d765a8-49a7-586e-bf26-cb4258bf6426" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37778/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "7f2e5de8-8541-5289-9b1f-2a42c7bdfad0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37778/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "5b191a5e-4e66-5b6c-97fa-c9f6f41f7fe7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37778/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "187c4fed-3a95-5a17-bbf9-edfe06c0c00a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37778/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f10012ac-3daa-5e5c-a450-09ea1565025f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37778/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer-field/choices ["q-37778/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" "q-37778/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-37778/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-37778/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-37778/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37778" :question/id #uuid "d3dc3dd7-99d0-56d1-a9a1-9893c6a8f904" :question/math-academy-id "q-37778" :question/problem "Given that $\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,{A}^{-1}=pI+qA$, find the value $p+q.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's find the characteristic equation $\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2}-4A+I & =O.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A$ is invertible, we can multiply this equation by ${A}^{-1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1}({A}^{2}-4A+I) & =O \\\\ A-4I+{A}^{-1} & =O \\\\ {A}^{-1} & =4I-A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $p=4,$ $q=-1$ and\n\n$$\np+q=4+(-1)=3.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-37778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "152243fa-e0a5-551d-92d9-b470789087c7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844/selection/fcc08ab77612b5f1df1a91786c225ae700d1b7387e53b0aa6ac17a11dcbb0973" :answer/id #uuid "60e1ab85-315f-5f4b-bf3d-d65e6efe54fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}40 & 24 \\\\ -70 & -44\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844/selection/4f4a05c871c858606340eb6e4be58b0dbe01d71e4523e2eb4a0816c57cb96a03" :answer/id #uuid "162bd55a-e089-5985-93cd-731277d307ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844/selection/bb2e076d977a02e3aa8079eb8bc6c13217b240c410291667ddd0280a1c33db8c" :answer/id #uuid "fbcab531-5c2e-5929-a23e-29a91fa14572" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}16 & -25 \\\\ 18 & -42\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844/selection/b6e932be7d80249ee2c1e7725a90829759db622eaa493bd321121b25fa812481" :answer/id #uuid "bcdbba2a-4104-51db-8f18-902512052921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844/selection/8c5d3391555610365a33dbe7a07ffe371179d0e5bf767965ef9ccc4fdf128b30" :answer/id #uuid "9b899ec5-e738-51b1-b357-d164f8adac01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & -24 \\\\ 8 & -16\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d5246b3e-19b7-5392-bdbb-9be88550808f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37844/selection/b6e932be7d80249ee2c1e7725a90829759db622eaa493bd321121b25fa812481" :answer-field/choices ["q-37844/selection/fcc08ab77612b5f1df1a91786c225ae700d1b7387e53b0aa6ac17a11dcbb0973" "q-37844/selection/4f4a05c871c858606340eb6e4be58b0dbe01d71e4523e2eb4a0816c57cb96a03" "q-37844/selection/bb2e076d977a02e3aa8079eb8bc6c13217b240c410291667ddd0280a1c33db8c" "q-37844/selection/b6e932be7d80249ee2c1e7725a90829759db622eaa493bd321121b25fa812481" "q-37844/selection/8c5d3391555610365a33dbe7a07ffe371179d0e5bf767965ef9ccc4fdf128b30"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37844" :question/id #uuid "df379c8f-bbed-5154-8e34-f7aedf45ba74" :question/math-academy-id "q-37844" :question/problem "Given the matrix\n$\\,A=[\\begin{aligned}14 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14\\end{aligned}]$\nand $f(x)={x}^{12}-4{x}^{10}+{x}^{3}-2x-3$, find $f(A).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by finding the characteristic polynomial $p(\\lambda )$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p(\\lambda ) & =det(A-\\lambda I) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}14-\\lambda  & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(14-\\lambda )(-14-\\lambda )+192 \\\\  & ={\\lambda }^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's divide $f(x)$ by $p(x)$ using long division:\n\n|  | $\\,\\,{x}^{10}$ | $+$ | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${x}^{2}-4\\,$ | $\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{{x}^{12}-4{x}^{10}+{x}^{3}-2x-3}$ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | ${x}^{12}$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{10}$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  | ${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,2x$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3$ |\n|  |  |  |  | ${x}^{3}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,$ | $-\\,\\,$ | $\\,\\,4x$ |  |  |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  | $\\,\\,2x$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-$ | $\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3$ |\n\nTherefore, we can write $f(x)$ as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =q(x)p(x)+r(x) \\\\  & =q(x)p(x)+(2x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $q(x)={x}^{10}+x.$ Replacing $x$ with $A,$ we have\n\n$$\nf(A)=q(A)p(A)+(2A-3I).\n$$\n\nAccording to the Cayley-Hamilton theorem, we have $p(A)=O.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & =q(A)p(A)+(2A-3I) \\\\  & =q(A)\\cdot O+(2A-3I) \\\\  & =2A-3I \\\\  & =2[\\begin{aligned}14 & 8 \\\\ -24 & -14\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}28 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -28\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}25 & 16 \\\\ -48 & -31\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-37844/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "787173e1-f957-5ff0-9d14-a6ccb11de1d8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37844"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186125053 :question/answer-fields 17592186123340] {:db/id "q-38702/selection/ma-v1/e694cf07bf6f603d431aaddd99304eb29cc7ab8f382275b4a724bd2333b2389a/47660d7a716ee65538395511cf5f3212646ed1c427b60f67465770b1bc8701ba" :answer/id #uuid "695db959-36b3-562f-bc46-a97b55740392" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8A-12I" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38702/selection/ma-v1/e694cf07bf6f603d431aaddd99304eb29cc7ab8f382275b4a724bd2333b2389a/7f6138867fc28aafda45316a043b2f3b7ea3f8ff15ee86